WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.120
So now that you've built up your technical skills and you've got your offer

2
00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:03.760
taking shape,

3
00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:05.840
now it's time to put yourself out there.

4
00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:10.000
This week is about outreach and also the mindset that you need in order for you

5
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:11.200
to find success here

6
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:14.960
so that you can learn to see outreach as math instead of rejection and also how

7
00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:15.120
you can

8
00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:17.760
master warm outreach as well as cold outreach.

9
00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:21.040
All right, so before we talk tactics, we first need to talk about mindset

10
00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:21.680
because

11
00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:25.280
tactics without the right headspace is going to be useless for you.

12
00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:28.720
Yes, you'll learn a great strategy but then you never use it because something

13
00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:29.040
in the back

14
00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:30.800
of your mind tells you not to.

15
00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:34.880
And usually what I find with most new starters is that the reason is always

16
00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:35.440
emotional.

17
00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:39.270
So you may have some sort of fear of rejection or fear of looking stupid or

18
00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:39.760
fear of being

19
00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:43.840
a bit salesy and I've seen some peers go to entire courses and take perfect

20
00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:44.240
notes

21
00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:46.320
but they never really take any action.

22
00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:49.280
And so for those people, the knowledge really wasn't the problem.

23
00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:52.400
It's all about their headspace and the fact that they're not actually seeing

24
00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:54.400
the reality of how to get clients.

25
00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:57.440
So I think it's good to address that head-on and this varies per person.

26
00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:00.640
So it may not be as easy, but if you don't talk about it now, it will

27
00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:02.400
quietly kill your momentum later.

28
00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:05.950
And in my opinion, one of the strongest mindset shifts that change everything,

29
00:01:05.950 --> 00:01:06.720
at least for me,

30
00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:08.800
is to realize that everything is just math.

31
00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:12.400
And once you see it this way, you stop taking things personally and you start

32
00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:15.200
treating outreach like a system that you can tune.

33
00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:19.120
To give an example, if you send 100 direct messages and you get only one reply,

34
00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:20.640
you don't think of that as a failure.

35
00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:22.160
That's a 1% response rate.

36
00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:25.440
And so that is data and data is something that you can work with.

37
00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:28.000
Maybe you can tweak your message, maybe you target different people,

38
00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:32.160
and suddenly that click-through rate and that response rate suddenly increases.

39
00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:33.360
Same thing with conversations.

40
00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:37.190
If you have 10 conversations and you only close one client, that's a 10% close

41
00:01:37.190 --> 00:01:37.520
rate.

42
00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:39.920
And so let's say you want five clients as your target,

43
00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:43.120
then working backwards from that, then you need roughly 50 conversations.

44
00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:46.560
So the question now becomes how do I get in front of 50 people,

45
00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:50.560
which is a totally different problem to solve and is usually easier and is much

46
00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:51.280
more manageable,

47
00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:54.960
right? And this is key because numbers depersonalize rejection.

48
00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:58.080
When you see all of this as math, then whenever you receive a no,

49
00:01:58.080 --> 00:01:59.520
it doesn't mean that you're bad at this.

50
00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:03.040
It just means that that is one data point across the plethora of efforts

51
00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:04.240
that you will be giving here.

52
00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:06.640
And all you need to do is to start reading it well.

53
00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:09.120
So think about what went wrong, what could be better,

54
00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:11.200
and that's how you get sharper with every attempt.

55
00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:13.600
Remember that a 1% improvement every day,

56
00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:15.600
if you compound that over the course of the year,

57
00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:20.000
you will end up with a 37x multiplier versus what you were at the beginning of

58
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:20.320
the year.

59
00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:23.760
And so with these sorts of systems, outreach for clients included,

60
00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:26.480
it's more about staying the course and being consistent with it,

61
00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:28.720
versus wanting to perfect it at the very beginning.

62
00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:32.000
So what you need to do to drive this home further is you should be tracking

63
00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:32.720
what we call

64
00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:36.800
input KPIs, key performance indicators, and not output KPIs.

65
00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:38.800
You need to detach yourself from the outcome,

66
00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:40.480
which is sometimes counterintuitive,

67
00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:43.040
but if you track your inputs instead of your outputs,

68
00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:45.360
that actually puts you in a position of control.

69
00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:48.480
But if you're like most people who set a goal based on the things that they can

70
00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:48.880
control,

71
00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:52.720
basically the output KPI, like getting three clients this week, for example,

72
00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:54.320
you actually can't control that.

73
00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:57.040
It depends on other people saying yes at the right time.

74
00:02:57.040 --> 00:02:59.280
It depends on other circumstances,

75
00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:03.440
depending on your personal context to align so that you get that target.

76
00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:05.760
But what you can do is to track your input KPI,

77
00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:09.040
which is let's say if your target is to send 100 messages this week,

78
00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:11.280
then that is entirely something that you can control, right?

79
00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:12.000
It's just action.

80
00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:15.120
You either did the repetitions, you either did the reps, or you did it.

81
00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:16.960
There's no ambiguity to do this,

82
00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:19.360
and there's no waiting around for someone else to respond.

83
00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:22.000
And so with the actions that you're going to take in this course,

84
00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:23.760
always have that shirt in mindset.

85
00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:27.120
So for example, if you want to target to book two calls this week,

86
00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:30.720
actually flip that and reverse it so that you send 10 DMs a day,

87
00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:31.920
something that you can control.

88
00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:34.000
If you want to have five conversations this week,

89
00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:36.240
then focus on the number of messages that you send,

90
00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:39.440
and then just work backwards to see once you do enough volume,

91
00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:42.320
what is your conversion rate in that whole metric,

92
00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:45.600
and see how many conversations you get coming from the messages that you send.

93
00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:49.040
And so let's say these are your numbers with roughly around 50 messages sent.

94
00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:52.080
You got three conversations, then that means that the next week,

95
00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:56.000
if you want to have more than five conversations as sort of your output metric,

96
00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:57.600
you simply need to double your inputs.

97
00:03:57.600 --> 00:03:58.640
That's all there is to it.

98
00:03:58.640 --> 00:04:01.200
And that is a much cleaner question to address, usually,

99
00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:03.760
versus thinking about how can I get more conversation,

100
00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:05.520
or how can I get more clients.

101
00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:09.400
The other thing that you might be worried with is about being annoying or spam

102
00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:09.760
my,

103
00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:10.880
especially in the next module,

104
00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:14.720
when we actually start to use our own personal contacts in order to reach out

105
00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:15.280
to people,

106
00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:18.480
to let them know that we have a service life to offer AI agents,

107
00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:21.040
you might feel a bit weird that you are reaching out to these people

108
00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:22.720
for a new service that you are offering.

109
00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:26.540
But you'll find later on that the key here is that the intention always makes

110
00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:27.040
the difference,

111
00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:29.840
and you need to trust that the skill that you built up for yourself

112
00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:31.280
is actually helpful for people.

113
00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:34.160
And getting the word out there is going to open up doors for you,

114
00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:37.600
and also be valuable for the people that you are offering this to.

115
00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:40.880
And anyways, spam is just blasting relevant messages to people who don't care,

116
00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:41.040
right?

117
00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:42.560
But even for cold outreach,

118
00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:44.960
where you send messages to people that you don't know,

119
00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:46.000
practically strangers,

120
00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:48.080
you can find ways, and we'll tackle this later on,

121
00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:51.200
on how you can add value that will just let people trust you more,

122
00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:54.560
and have confidence that you can actually solve their specific problem.

123
00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:57.120
So even if we do outreach and messaging at scale,

124
00:04:57.120 --> 00:04:58.640
if you lead with something useful,

125
00:04:58.640 --> 00:05:01.360
like for example, an audit, a mockup of a design,

126
00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:03.360
or an insight that they didn't ask for,

127
00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:05.280
but are glad that they got, then it's okay.

128
00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:08.800
And finally, what you need to realize is that the goal is conversations.

129
00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:11.200
We're not closing yet, we'll tackle that at a later stage.

130
00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:14.720
What you need to do for this week is to try to have a conversation.

131
00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:16.480
So you need to take the pressure off yourself.

132
00:05:16.480 --> 00:05:18.560
You don't need to be a salesperson right now.

133
00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:21.280
You don't need to close and sign a client right now.

134
00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:23.840
What you just need is to get that conversation flowing,

135
00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:24.880
get your practice in,

136
00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:27.600
in terms of how to pitch yourself and how to pitch your service,

137
00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:29.520
and just become someone worth talking to.

138
00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:30.800
So having a signed contract,

139
00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:31.840
sending an invoice,

140
00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:35.520
the structure of how we're actually going to deliver AI agents for people,

141
00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:37.200
is all going to be tackled separately.

142
00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:40.240
But this week, just focus on having that conversation.

143
00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:42.640
So as you do the necessary actions for this week,

144
00:05:42.640 --> 00:05:44.560
remember that it's all just math.

145
00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:45.600
Rejection is data.

146
00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:48.880
Your inputs are what's key and conversations are the goal.

147
00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:51.360
So if you walk away from this module with just those things,

148
00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:53.920
then you're already ahead of 90% of people

149
00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:56.400
who never start because they're too stuck in their own head.

150
00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:58.880
So next we'll be talking about warm outreach,

151
00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:02.240
which in my view is the fastest path to your first client.
